{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.PairingVariationalDerivative","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.PairingVariationalDerivative","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.BilinearMap","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.FrobeniusPairingCategorical"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.contractionAction_variation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.contractionAction_variation","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L325-L335","doc":"**The punchline, on the corpus's own ingredients.**  The action here is\nnothing but the corpus's scalar, squared — and its variational derivative is\nstill a bilinear form on the rank-2 pairing field space.  Compare\n`ExternalCurrents.einsteinTensor`, which stores one value of `η ≫ T` and\ntherefore cannot carry this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.contractionAction_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.contractionAction_value","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L318-L323","doc":"The contraction action's value: the square of the scalar the corpus keeps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.contractionAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.contractionAction","kind":"def","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L305-L316","doc":"**Existence constructor for `PairingFieldAction`**, built only from\ningredients the corpus already has: contract a rank-2 pairing field against a\nco-pairing `η`, read the resulting scalar with `ε`, and square it.\n\nThis is the wiring the corpus's `HasAction` could not carry.  `HasAction`\nhas no instance anywhere, and could not usefully have one: its domain is\n`End(𝟙_C)`, so there is nothing to vary.  Here the same scalar data produces\nan action on the **pairings**, and `QuadraticAction.ofFunctional_variation`\nthen gives it a rank-2 variational derivative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.exists_contract_not_reflecting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.exists_contract_not_reflecting","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L298-L303","doc":"Contrapositive form: two distinct rank-2 fields that a contraction cannot\ntell apart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.subsingleton_of_contract_reflects","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.subsingleton_of_contract_reflects","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L283-L296","doc":"**A scalar contraction cannot state a rank-2 identity.**  If equality of\ncontractions implied equality of the rank-2 fields, uniformly in the\nco-pairing, then there would be at most one pairing `dual ⊗ obj ⟶ 𝟙_ C`.\n\nThe invariant is `zero_comp`: the degenerate co-pairing `η = 0` contracts\nevery rank-2 field to the same scalar, so it separates nothing.  Hence in any\n`Preadditive` monoidal category whose pairing space has two distinct\nelements, a scalar-valued Einstein-shaped equation is **strictly weaker**\nthan the rank-2 identity it is named after. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.contract_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.contract_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L275-L281","doc":"**The scalar equation is the rank-2 equation modulo the kernel of the\ncontraction.**  This is exactly what the corpus's scalar Einstein slot can\nexpress, and exactly what it loses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.contract_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.contract_apply","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L271-L273","doc":"Definitional unfolding, recorded for `simp`.  Not a mathematical claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.contract","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.contract","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L260-L269","doc":"**Contraction** of a rank-2 pairing field against a co-pairing\n`η : 𝟙_ C ⟶ dual ⊗ obj`, landing in the scalars `End(𝟙_C)` — which is where\nthe corpus's `einsteinTensor` slot lives.  `R`-linearity is the content: the\n`map_add'` and `map_smul'` fields are what make this a trace rather than an\narbitrary function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.ScalarFieldAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.ScalarFieldAction","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L254-L258","doc":"The shape `MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction` has: a functional on the **scalars**.\nIts `QuadraticAction.variation` is a bilinear form on `End(𝟙_C)`, and no\nchoice of such an action can produce a functional on pairings, because\nneither `obj` nor `dual` occurs in its type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.PairingFieldAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.PairingFieldAction","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L249-L252","doc":"The shape this file supplies: a quadratic action whose field space is the\nspace of **pairings**.  Its `QuadraticAction.variation` is a bilinear form on\npairings — a rank-2 object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.fieldSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.fieldSpace","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L243-L247","doc":"The **field space** of a Frobenius pairing datum: every pairing on the same\n`(dual, obj)` pair.  `Preadditive` makes it an additive group and\n`Linear R C` makes it an `R`-module, so `QuadraticAction` applies to it\ndirectly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.value_does_not_determine_variation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.value_does_not_determine_variation","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L220-L230","doc":"**The value of the action does not determine its variational derivative.**\nTwo fields with the same action have different derivatives, so no single\nscalar can carry the rank-2 content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.intMulForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.intMulForm","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L212-L218","doc":"Multiplication on `ℤ`, as a bilinear form.  Used only as a witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.instInhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.instInhabited","kind":"instance","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L199-L200","doc":"Non-vacuity: every field space carries at least the zero action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional_variation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional_variation","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L188-L197","doc":"**An action built entirely from a scalar reading still has a rank-2\nvariational derivative.**  `ofFunctional ε` never sees a field except through\nthe scalar `ε e`, yet its derivative is the bilinear form\n`(e, δ) ↦ 2 · ε e · ε δ` on the field space.  So the corpus's scalar-valued\n`einsteinTensor` slot is not defensible on the ground that \"the action is a\nscalar anyway\": the action is a scalar in *both* shapes, and only the domain\ndecides the rank of the derivative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional_value","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L183-L186","doc":"The action of `ofFunctional ε` is the square of the scalar reading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional_form","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L180-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L162-L178","doc":"The quadratic action `e ↦ (ε e) ^ 2` attached to a linear functional `ε` on\nthe field space.  This is the existence constructor: every field space\ncarrying a functional carries an action.\n\nIt is also the case that matters here.  `ε` is a **scalar** reading of a\nfield, so this action is built entirely out of scalars — and\n`ofFunctional_variation` shows its variational derivative is a bilinear form\non the field space all the same.  Rank-2-ness comes from *what is varied*,\nnever from what the action's values are. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.polarization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.polarization","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L148-L154","doc":"**Polarization.**  The rank-2 derivative is recoverable from the action —\nbut only from the action as a *function on the whole field space*, never\nfrom its value at a single field.  Compare\n`value_does_not_determine_variation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.euler","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L141-L146","doc":"**Euler contraction.**  Contracting the variational derivative at `e` with\nthe field `e` itself returns the action, up to the degree factor `2`.  This\nis the sense in which a scalar is recovered from the rank-2 derivative — and\nthe coefficient is what the statement asserts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.value_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.value_smul","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L136-L139","doc":"**Degree-2 homogeneity.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.value_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.value_add","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L125-L134","doc":"**Exact Taylor identity.**  This is what makes `variation` *the* variational\nderivative rather than an arbitrary bilinear form: the first-order term of\n`value` at `e` in the direction `δ` is `variation e δ`, with the second-order\nremainder exactly `value δ`.  The identity fails for any other coefficient in\n`variation`, and its proof uses `form_symm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.variation_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.variation_apply","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L122-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.variation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.variation","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L117-L120","doc":"The **variational derivative**, as a bilinear form on the field space.\n`Q.variation e : V →ₗ[R] R` is the derivative at the field `e`; `Q.variation`\nitself is rank-2 *because the field space is*, not by stipulation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.value","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L114-L115","doc":"The action functional: a **scalar**, as an action should be. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.form_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.form_symm","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The form is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.form","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L106-L106","doc":"The bilinear form whose diagonal is the action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction","kind":"structure","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FrobeniusHopfData/PairingVariationalDerivative.lean#L98-L108","doc":"A **quadratic action functional** on a field space `V`: a symmetric\n`R`-bilinear form.  The action of a field `e` is `form e e`.\n\nThis is the shape `MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction` should have had: the domain of\nthe functional is the field space, not the scalars. ","signatureChunk":0}]}